+            title="The machine roll to Talos $VERSION stopped on $MACHINE"
+            what="**$MACHINE is left cordoned**, deliberately: nothing is retried, and a machine that will not come back is replaced rather than repaired. The machines before it are on $VERSION."
+            if [ -n "$REVERT" ]; then
+              what="$what A revert of the bump is open, unmerged: $REVERT"
+            else
+              what="$what There is no revert: the bump crosses a minor version, and Talos goes forward only. Fix forward."
+            fi
+            labels="priority:P1,type:correctness,epoch:05"
+          else
+            title="The machine roll to Talos $VERSION has not started"
+            what="**Nothing was touched.** The roll refused before its first machine, and asks again in the next window."
+            labels="priority:P2,type:correctness,epoch:05"
+          fi
+          body="$(printf '%s\n' "$what" "" "The roll's own words, where it stopped:" "" '```' "$why" '```' "" "Run: $RUN_URL")"
+          # One issue for a roll that will not start, not one an hour: the
+          # same refusal tomorrow is a comment on today's.
+          existing=$(gh issue list --state open --search "in:title \"$title\"" --json number --jq '.[0].number // empty')
+          if [ -n "$existing" ]; then
+            gh issue comment "$existing" --body "$body"
+          else
+            gh issue create --title "$title" --label "$labels" --body "$body"
+          fi
+
